   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": "Rice and salmon",
   "part_id": "part-rice-and-salmon",
   "time": "~40 min, mostly waiting",
   "time_html": "<span>~40 min, mostly waiting</span>",
   "title": "Salt the salmon",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"150\">150 g</span> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"1\" data-f=\"fillet|fillets\" data-n=\"1\">1 fillet</span>)",
     "name_html": "Salmon fillet, skin on"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Sake"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Kosher salt (salmon)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Heat a fish grill (or a grill pan or frying pan) over <b>medium</b> heat.</li><li>Skin side down first, about 4 minutes, until the skin is crisp and golden.</li><li>Turn and cook about 4 minutes more, until the flesh is just opaque and flakes apart but still <b>moist</b> in the middle. Don’t take it to dry.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium",
    "label_html": "<span>medium</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-3",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Grill — stop while it's juicy",
