  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Wet your palms, dip 2–3 fingertips in the salt and rub it over both palms.</li><li>Take about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"100\" data-s=\"0\">100 g</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"cup\" data-a=\"0.5\" data-s=\"0\" data-alt=\"1\">½ cup</span>)</span> of the warm salmon rice in your left palm and press a small well in the middle.</li><li>Spoon in about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 tsp</span> of cold ikura — a little cluster in the <b>center</b>, not scattered through the rice.</li><li>Close the rice over it and press the triangle: right hand bent into a “mountain” on top, left hand cupping, turning a third each time — light, so it stays airy (see the <a href=\"onigiri.html\">onigiri page</a>).</li><li>Wrap a nori strip round the bottom if you like. Re-wet and re-salt your hands for each one. Eat warm or at room temperature, within a few hours.</li></ul>",
